    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d305-a2-a1">

                <pb facs="0586" n="516" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg516"/>

                <head>[First indorsement.]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Headquarters
                            Military Division Missouri</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Chicago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-03-14"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 14,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Respectfully referred to the commanding general, Department of Dakota, for
                    investigation and report, attention being invited to the statement contained in
                    the letter of A. R. Macdonell, inspector, commanding mounted police Northwestern
                    Territory, Wood Mountain.</p>
                <p>The commanding general, Department of Dakota, will please cause a careful
                    statement to be made of the number of half-breeds and Canadian Indians who have
                    been in the Milk River country and on the reservation referred to, and return
                    these papers with a full and detailed report as possible to these
                    headquarters.</p>
                <p>By command of Lieutenant-General Sheridan.</p>
                <closer><signed>R. WILLIAMS</signed>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Assistant
                        Adjutant-General.</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
